{
  "id": "halden-border-human-red",
  "title": "Halden border — Red played by a person",
  "description": "Halden border for two sides: Blue runs civil dispatch and the defence of Objective KNUT while a second player commands Red's recce and four tanks. Red decides when and how to attack: its calls are an attack on KNUT that needs two tanks and a scouting task, and it sees Blue only through its own recce and tanks, as Blue sees Red only through its observation post and recce. Blue's calls follow the same timeline as the scripted exercise. A fictional exercise around Halden with no national markings: calls, forces and numbers are authored for play, not claims about real services or armed forces. How to play: Blue picks \"Blue (one person)\" or splits \"Civil desks\" and \"Blue military\", and Red picks \"Red commander\" on another iPad; the role chip reopens the groups dialog. Tap a call to see its suggested units and tap Dispatch to send them. Tap one of your units to highlight it, then tap a call, a place or an identified enemy to send it there. + on a unit's row adds the next target you tap to the end of its chain, so Red can route its tanks through waypoints before the attack.",
  "objectives": [
    "Blue: dispatch every call, all closed by 35:00, and reach the 25:00 top-priority call within six minutes.",
    "Blue: hold Objective KNUT, so Red never completes its attack.",
    "Red: take Objective KNUT, two tanks completing the Attack call.",
    "Red: lose fewer steps than Blue."
  ],
